# Vectorize visibility work by default

If a path will touch more than a toy number of visibility rows, do not write a
Python `for row in ...` estimator, interpolator, or geometry walk.

Use NumPy/JAX batch kernels as the first implementation, not as a later
optimization. A one-core CPython loop on Bacchus is a bug even when it is
scientifically correct.

Existing per-row helpers may be used only on already-reduced samples or in
unit tests. Do not call them from HOLORASTER-scale recover or predict paths.
